                <pb facs="0915" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/424: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-21T18:00:00-05:00">December 21, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Your 75, December 17, 2 p.m. The Department feels that you should avoid
                    advising the Chinese Government with respect to specific measures but you may
                    emphasize the urgent and vital considerations <pb facs="0916" n="909"
                        xml:id="pg909"/> involved, bearing in mind the general objectives of the
                    Department’s telegram no. 339, December 12, 3 p.m., to the American Embassy in
                    Tokyo. For your information there is given below the text of a telegram being
                    sent to the American Embassy in Tokyo:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of Department’s telegram No. 366, December 21, 6 p.m.,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
